# CLAIMS

**Claim 1.** An electromagnetic actuator system comprising:

an electromagnetic actuator having a coil configured to receive an electrical current for generating an electromagnetic force;

a current sensor configured to measure the electrical current supplied to the coil and generate a current signal indicative thereof;

a timing module configured to determine a time duration associated with application of the electrical current to the coil;

a processing unit communicatively coupled to the current sensor and the timing module, the processing unit configured to:

calculate a current-time evaluation product based on the current signal and the time duration;

compare the calculated current-time evaluation product against a predefined limit value; and

generate an error signal indicative of a fault condition when the calculated current-time evaluation product exceeds the predefined limit value.

**Claim 2.** The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1, wherein the processing unit is further configured to calculate the current-time evaluation product by integrating the current signal over the time duration.

**Claim 3.** The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1, wherein the predefined limit value is determined based on at least one of a thermal characteristic of the coil, a rated operating current of the electromagnetic actuator, or a manufacturer-specified duty cycle limit.

**Claim 4.** The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1, further comprising a control module configured to interrupt the electrical current supplied to the coil in response to the error signal.

**Claim 5.** The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1, wherein the processing unit is further configured to store the calculated current-time evaluation product in a memory for subsequent diagnostic evaluation.

**Claim 6.** The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1, wherein the fault condition corresponds to at least one of an overcurrent condition, a stalled actuator condition, or a mechanical binding condition.

**Claim 7.** A method for detecting a fault condition in an electromagnetic actuator, the method comprising:

measuring, via a current sensor, an electrical current supplied to a coil of the electromagnetic actuator;

determining a time duration over which the electrical current is applied to the coil;

calculating, via a processing unit, a current-time evaluation product based on the measured electrical current and the determined time duration;

comparing the calculated current-time evaluation product against a predefined limit value; and

generating an error signal indicative of the fault condition when the calculated current-time evaluation product exceeds the predefined limit value.

**Claim 8.** The method of claim 7, further comprising interrupting the electrical current supplied to the coil in response to generating the error signal.

**Claim 9.** The method of claim 7, wherein calculating the current-time evaluation product comprises integrating a magnitude of the electrical current over the time duration.

**Claim 10.** The method of claim 7, further comprising adjusting the predefined limit value based on an operating temperature of the electromagnetic actuator.

**Claim 11.** A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by a processing unit, cause the processing unit to:

receive a current signal indicative of an electrical current supplied to a coil of an electromagnetic actuator;

receive a time duration signal indicative of a time duration over which the electrical current is applied to the coil;

calculate a current-time evaluation product based on the current signal and the time duration signal;

compare the calculated current-time evaluation product against a predefined limit value; and

output an error signal indicative of a fault condition when the calculated current-time evaluation product exceeds the predefined limit value.
